would welcome you back after this fiasco?

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:56.366
Take a few days off
and come back when things cool down.

00:18:56.449 --> 00:18:58.409
But his claim hasn't even been verified.

00:18:58.493 --> 00:19:00.787
He's talking about genetic testing,
but it can't be legally enforced!

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:02.997
It's obvious he'll keep putting it off
until it never happens!

00:19:03.081 --> 00:19:05.500
Also, he got the party nomination
and might run in the by-election--

00:19:05.583 --> 00:19:06.751
Here.

00:19:06.834 --> 00:19:07.794
Read it.

00:19:14.050 --> 00:19:15.259
GENETIC TEST REPORT

00:19:17.887 --> 00:19:19.222
PROBABILITY OF PATERNITY: 99.999%

00:19:20.473 --> 00:19:21.766
I have to issue a correction?

00:19:21.849 --> 00:19:24.227
Do you expect me to issue a correction
for an article you wrote?

00:19:24.811 --> 00:19:26.562
We have to issue a correction first

00:19:26.646 --> 00:19:27.939
before he drops the lawsuit.

00:19:43.204 --> 00:19:44.038
Ms. Wi.

00:19:48.209 --> 00:19:49.043
Have you eaten yet?

00:19:49.627 --> 00:19:51.421
-No.
-Then let's go eat.

00:19:52.547 --> 00:19:54.173
Do I look like the starving type?

00:19:55.299 --> 00:19:57.844
You keep vanishing
every time I invite you to eat.

00:19:58.803 --> 00:20:00.722
Promise that you'll eat with me today.

00:20:04.767 --> 00:20:06.602
Co-produce Kang Pil-gu?

00:20:06.686 --> 00:20:08.021
You're going into producing, Mr. Hwang?

00:20:10.398 --> 00:20:11.482
Yes, well…

00:20:12.066 --> 00:20:15.862
I thought I'd start out with this project.

00:20:17.321 --> 00:20:20.575
I guess it's trendy for agencies
to get into production.

00:20:20.658 --> 00:20:24.829
Well, actors don't just want to sit around
and wait for offers to come in.

00:20:24.912 --> 00:20:28.708
They feel an urge to make something
on their own every now and then.

00:20:30.293 --> 00:20:32.253
This isn't a decision
I can make on my own.

00:20:32.336 --> 00:20:34.297
I'll talk it over with my company.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:35.423
Right.

00:20:36.382 --> 00:20:39.302
And about Director Bak…

00:20:39.385 --> 00:20:40.887
-Director Bak Byeong-gi?
-Yes.

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:43.723
Gosh…

00:20:43.806 --> 00:20:45.892
Go ahead and say it.

00:20:45.975 --> 00:20:47.393
-Well…
-Go ahead.

00:20:47.477 --> 00:20:49.479
You see, Director Bak used to be

00:20:49.562 --> 00:20:54.400
a very promising young director,

00:20:54.484 --> 00:20:57.028
but he hasn't directed in so long…

00:20:57.111 --> 00:21:00.156
-That's not true.
-That's an excellent point.

00:21:01.115 --> 00:21:05.036
Director Bak is the genius type, so it…

00:21:05.119 --> 00:21:07.330
So unlike the previous seasons,

00:21:07.413 --> 00:21:10.541
it's possible this season
could turn out to be very…

00:21:10.625 --> 00:21:12.627
Bak Byeong-gi is a total lunatic.

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:14.295
So we make one wrong move,

00:21:14.378 --> 00:21:17.173
and it might turn out downright bizarre.

00:21:17.256 --> 00:21:18.299
Is that okay with you?

00:21:18.382 --> 00:21:21.511
There's such a big difference in length
between movies and dramas,

00:21:21.594 --> 00:21:23.638
it could take him time to adjust to it.

00:21:23.721 --> 00:21:27.058
He films all day and night
in the name of art,

00:21:27.141 --> 00:21:29.227
so he'll go over
the time and budget limit.

00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:33.272
You'll need to do a really good job
putting together a key crew.

00:21:33.356 --> 00:21:35.817
The second unit director, gaffer,
director of photography, music director…

00:21:35.900 --> 00:21:38.319
I'm going to assign them myself.

00:21:38.402 --> 00:21:39.237
End of discussion.

00:21:40.321 --> 00:21:43.282
I mean, I still trust he'll do a good job,

00:21:43.366 --> 00:21:46.536
but I'm a little concerned.

00:21:51.249 --> 00:21:52.542
Come on, bro.

00:21:53.626 --> 00:21:56.045
Is it really our place
to assign the key crew?

00:21:56.129 --> 00:21:59.006
I'm not assigning anyone.
I'm merely suggesting.

00:21:59.090 --> 00:22:00.299
Oh, so you're suggesting.

00:22:00.383 --> 00:22:01.843
You watched The Days of Romance.

00:22:01.926 --> 00:22:05.429
Cinematographer Hwang Ji-hyeok
is amazing at shooting male actors.

00:22:05.513 --> 00:22:06.889
That was a melodrama.

00:22:06.973 --> 00:22:08.474
This is a detective action series.

00:22:08.558 --> 00:22:11.727
It's not important
that your face looks soft and dreamy.

00:22:13.646 --> 00:22:14.605
It's good, right?

00:22:16.482 --> 00:22:17.316
What is it?

00:22:19.152 --> 00:22:20.319
It's important to me.

00:22:20.403 --> 00:22:21.737
I'm determined to do a melodrama next.

00:22:22.321 --> 00:22:23.906
Fine. How about a round
at a golf simulator?

00:22:24.991 --> 00:22:26.742
I have an appointment with Byeong-gi.

00:22:28.119 --> 00:22:29.704
Why are you meeting with him?

00:22:30.496 --> 00:22:32.415
Why? Tell me.

00:22:32.999 --> 00:22:33.833
You must be upset

00:22:34.709 --> 00:22:36.294
about not returning to the political desk.

00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:40.339
I suppose so.

00:22:40.423 --> 00:22:43.759
The public reacted so badly
to the Yoon Jung-ho article

00:22:44.427 --> 00:22:45.970
that I couldn't do anything about it.

00:22:49.515 --> 00:22:50.600
But I have to say,

00:22:51.225 --> 00:22:52.268
I can't help feeling excited.

00:22:54.103 --> 00:22:55.438
I get to keep seeing you like this

00:22:55.521 --> 00:22:56.814
since you're not returning
to the political desk.

00:23:02.236 --> 00:23:03.321
ERADICATING DIGITAL SEX CRIMES

00:23:05.823 --> 00:23:07.158
SIMPLE AND EASY, TAILORED FIT!

00:23:19.503 --> 00:23:22.298
Are you a fan of Lim Hyeon-jun?

00:23:23.925 --> 00:23:24.759
No.

00:23:26.594 --> 00:23:28.804
Really? But you were staring at him.

00:23:29.305 --> 00:23:31.057
And at the baseball stadium too.

00:23:32.850 --> 00:23:35.269
Oh, did I? I don't remember.

00:23:37.396 --> 00:23:38.689
Hey, slow down.

00:23:41.317 --> 00:23:42.318
This is good.

00:23:42.401 --> 00:23:43.319
Yes, it is.

00:23:46.322 --> 00:23:48.616
When I said I felt excited earlier,

00:23:48.699 --> 00:23:49.742
you know I was joking, right?

00:23:52.161 --> 00:23:54.121
Seeing you having to stick around
because of the incident

00:23:55.498 --> 00:23:56.624
doesn't make me feel good.

00:23:58.209 --> 00:23:59.085
Because of me?

00:24:00.086 --> 00:24:00.920
Yes.

00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:08.761
Do you always worry about
any woman you see?

00:24:10.763 --> 00:24:13.307
Well, I've always had good manners,

00:24:14.308 --> 00:24:15.393
but I'm not that easy.

00:24:16.936 --> 00:24:18.729
Are you aware that you confuse people?

00:24:19.855 --> 00:24:22.400
I hear something's going on
between you and our chief.

00:24:23.276 --> 00:24:25.278
So let's not give anyone the wrong idea.

00:24:28.531 --> 00:24:30.950
I was in a relationship with her
a long time ago.

00:24:31.575 --> 00:24:34.120
I don't know what you heard,

00:24:35.496 --> 00:24:36.372
but we're not together now.

00:24:37.915 --> 00:24:40.376
Are you feeling jealous?

00:24:42.878 --> 00:24:44.213
It's not like that.

00:25:05.318 --> 00:25:08.321
BAK BYEONG-GI

00:25:15.953 --> 00:25:17.580
-Come in.
-Thanks.

00:25:20.374 --> 00:25:21.959
This is nice.

00:25:22.585 --> 00:25:24.337
When did you move to this studio?

00:25:25.004 --> 00:25:27.298
I needed a bigger place
because I have so many books.

00:25:27.381 --> 00:25:28.424
Would you like a beverage?

00:25:28.507 --> 00:25:29.842
-No.
-All right.

00:25:29.925 --> 00:25:32.345
Where's your assistant?
Why are you working alone?

00:25:32.428 --> 00:25:34.555
Everyone works from home these days.

00:25:36.140 --> 00:25:37.600
How much have you written so far?

00:25:38.184 --> 00:25:41.395
I sent in episodes five and six last week,
and now I'm writing seven and eight.

00:25:42.605 --> 00:25:46.025
Once we have the supporting cast and crew,
we'll need to start filming right away.

00:25:46.108 --> 00:25:47.318
Will that be enough?

00:25:47.401 --> 00:25:49.862
You won't have time to write
because of the shoot preparations.

00:25:49.945 --> 00:25:51.364
I'll have to make it happen.

00:25:54.700 --> 00:25:55.868
If you're having difficulty,

00:25:55.951 --> 00:25:58.245
how about getting a co-writer?

00:25:58.329 --> 00:25:59.163
A co-writer?

00:25:59.246 --> 00:26:00.122
Yeah.

00:26:00.623 --> 00:26:03.959
I can introduce you to someone
who's good at writing romantic lines.

00:26:04.710 --> 00:26:07.713
I've already mapped out the ending,
so it won't be hard to write the script.

00:26:07.797 --> 00:26:08.631
Don't worry about it.

00:26:13.719 --> 00:26:14.595
Oh, yeah?

00:26:15.846 --> 00:26:17.014
Well…

00:26:17.098 --> 00:26:19.266
I guess that's a relief.

00:26:21.102 --> 00:26:22.603
By the way,

00:26:22.686 --> 00:26:26.482
the premise of Kang Pil-gu
becoming a corrupt detective…

00:26:26.565 --> 00:26:28.943
Isn't that rather cliché?

00:26:30.403 --> 00:26:33.906
He takes part in a crime
to save his late colleague's sister.

00:26:33.989 --> 00:26:35.032
Do you not like it?

00:26:35.950 --> 00:26:39.120
You need to add something extra in there.

00:26:39.203 --> 00:26:40.329
Something extra?

00:26:43.791 --> 00:26:47.294
During the rescue sequence
of his colleague's kidnapped sister,

00:26:47.378 --> 00:26:48.796
how about…

00:26:48.879 --> 00:26:49.797
Mi-yeong!

00:26:55.594 --> 00:26:56.429
Mi-yeong.

00:26:59.098 --> 00:26:59.932
Mi-yeong.

00:27:06.689 --> 00:27:07.815
Cut!

00:27:08.607 --> 00:27:09.817
Bad take.

00:27:10.443 --> 00:27:11.610
Why?

00:27:13.529 --> 00:27:15.823
Is it a bit much?

00:27:23.289 --> 00:27:24.123
Out of the blue like that?

00:27:24.707 --> 00:27:26.667
Why would they French kiss
when they don't know each other?

00:27:26.750 --> 00:27:28.794
She's his colleague's sister,
and they're meeting for the first time.

00:27:28.878 --> 00:27:30.796
Then just set up a backstory.

00:27:30.880 --> 00:27:34.675
Maybe they were childhood friends,
or maybe Pil-gu saved her from drowning.

00:27:34.758 --> 00:27:35.885
There are a ton of ideas.

00:27:35.968 --> 00:27:37.094
But why is that necessary?

00:27:37.178 --> 00:27:39.346
The viewers want to see Kang Pil-gu
in a romantic role.

00:27:42.558 --> 00:27:44.643
You refuse all romantic scenes
with the female lead,

00:27:44.727 --> 00:27:47.062
but it's fine with a minor character?
That makes no sense.

00:27:48.606 --> 00:27:50.858
A writer's job is to
make sense of such things.

00:27:51.358 --> 00:27:52.276
Are you freaking serious?

00:27:53.777 --> 00:27:54.820
Did you just swear at me?

00:27:56.405 --> 00:27:58.157
I almost did, but no.

00:28:00.326 --> 00:28:02.745
I'll give it some thought.

00:28:03.621 --> 00:28:06.123
I'll think about how to add

00:28:07.458 --> 00:28:08.792
some romantic lines.

00:28:09.793 --> 00:28:11.003
Good.

00:28:11.086 --> 00:28:12.922
You're a good writer, Mr. Bak.

00:28:13.005 --> 00:28:15.090
Give it your best shot, all right?

00:28:15.674 --> 00:28:18.177
-So, shall we go out and eat now?
-No, thank you.

00:28:18.719 --> 00:28:21.514
I have way too much to do.

00:28:21.597 --> 00:28:23.057
Enjoy your meal.

00:28:32.274 --> 00:28:35.236
SPORTS EUNSEONG
WI JEONG-SIN

00:28:35.319 --> 00:28:37.071
REGARDING THE EXCLUSIVE
ON ACTOR YOON JUNG-HO

00:28:40.241 --> 00:28:42.368
SUBMIT TO DESK

00:28:45.412 --> 00:28:46.288
PUBLISH REQUEST SENT!

00:28:55.839 --> 00:28:57.758
REPORTER WI JEONG-SIN

00:29:16.443 --> 00:29:19.113
-This is Wi Jeong-sin speaking.
-It's me, Yoon Jung-ho.

00:29:19.697 --> 00:29:23.701
Perhaps you thought I'd drop the lawsuit
if you issued a correction,

00:29:23.784 --> 00:29:25.202
but I have no intention of doing so.

00:29:56.817 --> 00:29:57.860
This is Wi Jeong-sin speaking.

00:29:57.943 --> 00:29:59.528
I'd like to see you today.

00:30:00.738 --> 00:30:01.739
And who are you?

00:30:02.406 --> 00:30:05.409
At least identify yourself first
if you're the one who called!

00:30:10.164 --> 00:30:11.415
It's me, Lim Hyeon-jun.

00:30:13.459 --> 00:30:16.670
I thought for a second
that you had saved my number.

00:30:17.546 --> 00:30:20.549
But is that any reason
to answer a call like that?

00:30:21.800 --> 00:30:24.386
Anyway, I'm texting you an address.

00:30:24.470 --> 00:30:25.596
I'll see you there.

00:30:28.641 --> 00:30:29.475
Jeez.

00:30:43.030 --> 00:30:43.864
Is this his house?

00:31:13.018 --> 00:31:14.061
Why did you ask me here?

00:31:14.144 --> 00:31:16.313
To show off my house.

00:31:17.022 --> 00:31:18.232
It's nice, isn't it?

00:31:19.024 --> 00:31:19.858
Yes, it is.

00:31:20.859 --> 00:31:23.904
Jeez, you don't even understand a joke.

00:31:23.987 --> 00:31:26.615
It'll only cause a scandal
if people see us together in public.

00:31:30.953 --> 00:31:31.954
So, what's this about?

00:31:32.037 --> 00:31:34.164
You said I was like bad luck to you,
so I didn't expect to see you again.

00:31:34.748 --> 00:31:36.083
I never said you were bad luck.

00:31:37.126 --> 00:31:38.669
I said my life becomes a mess.

00:31:39.169 --> 00:31:40.212
That's even worse.

00:31:52.641 --> 00:31:54.226
So, about that former baseball player

00:31:54.935 --> 00:31:56.478
or media company president, or whatever.

00:31:57.062 --> 00:31:57.896
Are you two close?

00:31:59.398 --> 00:32:00.357
He's just my boss.

00:32:01.775 --> 00:32:03.485
Is there something
you want to know about him?

00:32:05.320 --> 00:32:06.697
Anyway,

00:32:07.656 --> 00:32:10.284
I asked you here
because I felt a bit of responsibility.

00:32:10.367 --> 00:32:12.995
I saw you issued a correction
about the Yoon Jung-ho article.

00:32:13.078 --> 00:32:14.413
Did he say he'd drop the lawsuit?

00:32:17.374 --> 00:32:19.001
Did you call because you were concerned?

00:32:25.340 --> 00:32:29.803
I mean, I participated
in that paparazzi mess, so…

00:32:31.930 --> 00:32:33.891
You're concerned you'll get humiliated.

00:32:33.974 --> 00:32:35.934
Just tell me what your next move is.

00:32:36.435 --> 00:32:39.021
-Why?
-Because I feel some responsibility!

00:32:39.980 --> 00:32:41.440
Okay, fine.

00:32:41.982 --> 00:32:44.109
I'll tell you your next move.

00:32:44.193 --> 00:32:45.778
Just start by apologizing.

00:32:45.861 --> 00:32:48.447
If you made a mistake,
you should apologize.

00:32:53.786 --> 00:32:54.912
I can't apologize.

00:32:56.413 --> 00:32:57.623
Not to that piece of trash.

00:32:57.706 --> 00:32:58.749
Piece of trash?

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:02.127
So you really won't apologize?

00:33:02.211 --> 00:33:03.545
I issued a correction

00:33:04.129 --> 00:33:06.256
and corrected my mistake as a reporter.

00:33:06.340 --> 00:33:07.299
I won't apologize personally.

00:33:08.717 --> 00:33:10.219
-Look--
-I'll make sure

00:33:10.302 --> 00:33:11.929
that you're not affected by this.

00:33:12.513 --> 00:33:14.640
-That's not the point--
-If we're done here,

00:33:15.432 --> 00:33:16.391
I'll be on my way.

00:33:17.935 --> 00:33:18.769
But…

00:33:24.942 --> 00:33:25.818
Seriously…

00:33:36.161 --> 00:33:37.120
Did you

00:33:37.204 --> 00:33:39.498
fail my brother at the audition
because of me?

00:33:41.041 --> 00:33:43.252
No, the thing is…

00:33:45.170 --> 00:33:47.840
Look, I don't let
petty emotions affect me.

00:33:47.923 --> 00:33:48.757
-The--
-If he couldn't act,

00:33:48.841 --> 00:33:50.008
you just had to fail him.

00:33:50.092 --> 00:33:51.510
Why did you have to rub salt in his wound?

00:33:51.593 --> 00:33:52.427
But that's not--

00:33:52.511 --> 00:33:54.930
Actors who go to auditions
are there to land a role,

00:33:55.430 --> 00:33:56.849
not to receive guidance.

00:33:56.932 --> 00:33:58.517
Exactly, so that's why I--

00:33:58.600 --> 00:33:59.601
Goodbye, then.

00:34:08.026 --> 00:34:09.528
Oh, boy.

00:34:12.656 --> 00:34:14.950
Everything is so messed up.

00:34:30.007 --> 00:34:32.050
What in the world is she thinking?

00:34:32.759 --> 00:34:36.054
She was bumped from the political desk
to the entertainment desk.

00:34:36.138 --> 00:34:38.181
If she leaves the entertainment desk,
then what?

00:34:38.265 --> 00:34:40.142
Where can she go?

00:35:03.790 --> 00:35:04.917
Damn it.

00:35:14.676 --> 00:35:15.886
Get in.

00:35:17.346 --> 00:35:19.222
Did you come out to give me a ride?

00:35:19.306 --> 00:35:21.183
No, I'm heading to the gym.

00:35:21.266 --> 00:35:22.851
Your home is on the way, so get in.

00:35:22.935 --> 00:35:24.645
You don't even know where I live.

00:35:24.728 --> 00:35:26.229
Are you refusing to get in, then?

00:35:44.790 --> 00:35:46.541
Stop wiping it down.

00:35:46.625 --> 00:35:47.918
It's fine.

00:35:48.627 --> 00:35:50.963
You should've just hopped in right away.

00:35:52.756 --> 00:35:53.632
Thank you.

00:35:54.925 --> 00:35:56.885
I know you're a busy man.
You should've just left.

00:35:58.261 --> 00:36:01.139
I knew you wouldn't have taken a taxi
or bought an umbrella.

00:36:01.223 --> 00:36:02.724
You would've just gotten soaked.

00:36:05.352 --> 00:36:06.228
How do you know?

00:36:07.646 --> 00:36:10.232
How do you know I wouldn't take a taxi
or buy an umbrella?

00:36:12.943 --> 00:36:14.820
I mean, it's obvious.

00:36:16.029 --> 00:36:17.030
You just look like the type.

00:36:21.827 --> 00:36:23.829
So how did you end up becoming a reporter?

00:36:24.371 --> 00:36:25.580
Why choose that over other jobs?

00:36:27.040 --> 00:36:28.375
It's a long story.

00:36:28.458 --> 00:36:29.626
Then make it short.

00:36:31.461 --> 00:36:35.632
Well, I had the looks,
but I also had the brains.

00:36:35.716 --> 00:36:38.218
I guess you could say
I was too perfect to be real.

00:36:38.301 --> 00:36:41.513
Gosh, I can't believe
your story begins with you showing off.

00:36:41.596 --> 00:36:42.681
Unbelievable.

00:36:42.764 --> 00:36:44.516
Go on. Continue.

00:36:45.600 --> 00:36:47.352
I was first in my class

00:36:48.020 --> 00:36:50.188
in elementary school,
middle school, and high school.

00:36:50.772 --> 00:36:51.898
But then…

00:36:51.982 --> 00:36:53.442
Second place?

00:36:54.317 --> 00:36:57.112
I was shocked
because I'd never come in second before.

00:36:57.195 --> 00:36:59.823
And I couldn't help but suspect the kid
who suddenly took the top of the class,

00:36:59.906 --> 00:37:02.534
when he had never once
made it into the top 30.

00:37:03.035 --> 00:37:06.288
So from that day on,
I started keeping an eye on him.

00:37:30.562 --> 00:37:31.646
And that's when I knew

00:37:32.481 --> 00:37:33.982
how he came out on top.

